{
    "background_story": "In the depths of the rainforest, there existed a rare and extraordinary plant species known as Luna. Its unique characteristic was the presence of cataphylls - modified leaves that protected its delicate buds from the harsh environment. As the seasons changed, Luna's cataphylls would unfurl, revealing vibrant, star-shaped flowers that shone like celestial bodies in the understory. Local botanists marveled at Luna's adaptations, which allowed it to thrive in the dense, shaded areas where light was scarce. Despite its elusive nature, Luna became a symbol of resilience and protection, reminding all who encountered it of the intricate relationships between plants and their surroundings. Its beauty and rarity earned it a revered place in the hearts of those who sought to preserve the rainforest's hidden treasures.",
